<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait bank assets rise in January month/month.</title>
<headline>Kuwait bank assets rise in January month/month.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of banks operating in Kuwait rose to 11.493 billion dinars at the end of January from 11.458 billion at the end of December, the Central Bank said in a monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.291 billion dinars in January 1996.</p>
<p>			Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>						Jan '97	   Jan '96</p>
<p> Cash					  61.0		 46.0</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	     8.9		 20.1</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	    1,762.2	    2,035.0</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		  2,752.7	    3,359.2</p>
<p> Other local investments		279.8		365.9</p>
<p>Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents			     3,265.2	    2,416.7</p>
<p> Foreign assets			 2,209.4	    2,040.7</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    697.7		526.4</p>
<p> Other assets			     456.0		480.6</p>
<p> Total				   11,493.0	   11,290.7</p>
<p>Note: Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.303 dinar)</p>
<p>Inal Ersan +965-243-1920</p>
